name cleveref-usedon
category Package
revision 70491
shortdesc Adds forward-referencing functionality to the cleveref package
relocated 1
longdesc Imagine you are reading a long mathematical text such as a text
longdesc book or a thesis. There are plenty of supplementary lemmas,
longdesc propositions, theorems and/or exercises throughout the whole
longdesc text. You ask yourself "Gosh, while Lemma 1.12 is certainly an
longdesc interesting result, where is this result used later on in this
longdesc long text? I really would find that helpful to decide why I
longdesc should read the proof." You can, of course, use the PDF search
longdesc function of your viewer to look up the string "Lemma 1.12", but
longdesc wouldn't it be more helpful if Lemma 1.12 already indicated all
longdesc or at least its most useful/crucial applications via an info
longdesc message? This is what this package tries to address: The info
longdesc message "Used on p. 40, 43-45 and 101." would then be printed
longdesc to the header of Lemma 1.12. This is done by extending the
longdesc \cref and \Cref commands and giving them an optional argument
longdesc UsedOn. Every time you wish to record a reference in the "used
longdesc on page list", you would simply type
longdesc \cref[UsedOn]{<LabelName>}. If you use \cref without this
longdesc optional argument, this reference won't be recorded in this
longdesc page list.
runfiles size=3
 RELOC/tex/latex/cleveref-usedon/cleveref-usedon.sty
